  "id": "desynchronization",
  "term": "desynchronization",
  "definition": "In this context, desynchronization refers to a drop in the power of a brain rhythm seen on EEG during an event or task. For the mu rhythm, event-related desynchronization is the suppression of activity around 8–13 Hz during movement, making it a marker of motor execution and planning.",
